          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Chapter Summary"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.543,
            0.883,
            0.622
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Quadrilateral:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " For four distinct points A, B, C, D in a plane with no three collinear, the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "quadrilateral",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ABCD is a collection of all points on segments AB, BC, CD, DA provided every point other than A, B, C, and D lies on exactly one of these four segments."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.625,
            0.881,
            0.666
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A quadrilateral is "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "convex",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " when all of its internal angles are less than 180°, or equivalently, when its diagonals intersect."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.67,
            0.881,
            0.707
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• The following converse statements about parallelograms are true:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.708,
            0.881,
            0.746
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "⸰ If the opposite sides of a 4-gon are equal, then it is a parallelogram."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.746,
            0.881,
            0.784
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If the opposite angles of a 4-gon are equal, then it is a parallelogram."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.784,
            0.881,
            0.823
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "⸰ If the diagonals of a 4-gon bisect each other, then it is a parallelogram."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.822,
            0.88,
            0.862
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "⸰ If a pair of opposite sides of a 4-gon are equal and parallel, then it is a parallelogram."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
